###  Summary


This receiver replaces `ExpressReceiver` as the default receiver for `App`. The main difference is that it does not depend on `express` and therefore is much less opinionated and more flexible.

The `receiver.httpListener` public property is a function that can used with any HTTP framework, or the standard `http/s.createServer()`. For example, you can use Bolt with your own server like so:

```
const { App, HTTPReceiver } = require('@slack/bolt');
const { createServer } = require('http');

const receiver = new HTTPReceiver(/* ... */);
const bolt = new App({ receiver, /* ... */ });

// Initialize your own server
const server = createServer((req, res) => {
  // In the real world you'd likely create other routes besides just this listener.
  try {
    receiver.requestListener(req, res);
  } catch (error) {
  }
});
```

For more details, see #670.

